  "markdownContent": "# German 1: Hallo! Greetings and sein\n\nSay hello and goodbye, introduce yourself, say where you come from, and meet the verb sein (to be).\n\n## Words\n\n| Word | Plural | Meaning | Pronunciation |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Hallo | — | hello | /ˈhalo/ |\n| tschüss | — | bye | /tʃʏs/ |\n| danke | — | thank you | /ˈdaŋkə/ |\n| bitte | — | please; you're welcome | /ˈbɪtə/ |\n| ja | — | yes | /jaː/ |\n| nein | — | no | /naɪ̯n/ |\n| der Name | die Namen | name | /ˈnaːmə/ |\n| der Herr | die Herren | Mr; gentleman | /hɛʁ/ |\n| die Frau | die Frauen | Mrs; woman | /fʁaʊ̯/ |\n| der Tag | die Tage | day | /taːk/ |\n| sein | — | to be | /zaɪ̯n/ |\n| heißen | — | to be called | /ˈhaɪ̯sn̩/ |\n| kommen | — | to come | /ˈkɔmən/ |\n\n## Phrases\n\n- **Guten Morgen!**: Good morning!\n- **Wie heißt du?**: What is your name?\n- **Ich heiße Anna.**: My name is Anna.\n- **Woher kommst du?**: Where are you from?\n- **Ich komme aus Deutschland.**: I come from Germany.\n- **Wie geht es dir?**: How are you?\n- **Mir geht es gut, danke.**: I am fine, thanks.\n- **Wir sind Freunde.**: We are friends.\n\n## Grammar: sein (to be)\n\n| Person | sein |\n| --- | --- |\n| ich | bin |\n| du | bist |\n| er / sie / es | ist |\n| wir | sind |\n| ihr | seid |\n| sie / Sie | sind |\n\n- **du** is for friends, family and children; **Sie** (always capitalized) is the polite form for adults you don't know.\n- Professions and nationalities take no article: *Ich bin Student.* (not *ein Student* in everyday speech).\n- Every noun is capitalized: *der Name, die Frau, der Tag*.\n",
